EXPERIMENT 30 – BRANCH COVERAGE TESTING USING JUNIT
AIM
To write JUnit test cases to achieve branch coverage on a program that finds the largest of three numbers using JUnit.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the JUnit 5 junit-jupiter dependency to pom.xml.
2. Create the MaxFinder class with the largest(a, b, c) method.
3. Identify the decisions: a >= b, a >= c and b >= c.
4. List the branches. Each decision must execute once as true and once as false.
5. Write four tests to execute every return statement:
   - A is largest.
   - C is largest when A is greater than or equal to B.
   - B is largest.
   - C is largest when B is greater than A.
6. Add one more test with three equal numbers.
7. Run tests using mvn test and verify branch coverage.
CODE
MaxFinder.java
public class MaxFinder {
    public static int largest(int a, int b, int c) {
        if (a >= b) {
            if (a >= c) {
                return a;
            } else {
                return c;
            }
        } else {
            if (b >= c) {
                return b;
            } else {
                return c;
            }
        }
    }
}


MaxFinderTest.java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class MaxFinderTest {

    @Test
    void aIsLargest() {
        assertEquals(9, MaxFinder.largest(9, 5, 3));
    }

    @Test
    void cIsLargestWhenAGreaterThanB() {
        assertEquals(9, MaxFinder.largest(5, 3, 9));
    }

    @Test
    void bIsLargest() {
        assertEquals(9, MaxFinder.largest(3, 9, 5));
    }

    @Test
    void cIsLargestWhenBGreaterThanA() {
        assertEquals(9, MaxFinder.largest(3, 5, 9));
    }

    @Test
    void allNumbersEqual() {
        assertEquals(4, MaxFinder.largest(4, 4, 4));
    }
}


INPUT
Test Case	a	b	c	Expected Output
A is largest	9	5	3	9
C is largest when A ≥ B	5	3	9	9
B is largest	3	9	5	9
C is largest when B > A	3	5	9	9
All numbers equal	4	4	4	4

